{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Working Hard"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Lunch Break"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 9}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe  necessity, duty, advice, or strong dissaproval in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "condensed"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "reduced"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Tell me all about it, the condensed version."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about professions and work responsibilities. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to see through"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to complete"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I've got a lot of tasks to see through this week."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "systematically"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " carefully; following a system"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I've got to work systematically."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob05aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to buckle down"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to focus on a task"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You have to buckle down Kristi, and get it done. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob05aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "accountability"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "responsibility"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He's thinking about giving you more accountability."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob05aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "overwhelmed"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "under pressure"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm starting to feel overwhelmed."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob05aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "liability"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that \u200bmight cause legal \u200btrouble"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have to fact-check the manuscript and look for copyright liability."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob05aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to get in over one's head"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to get involved in a difficult situation that you can't get out of"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's exciting but I've got to make sure I don't get in over my head."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob05aud08"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le09ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Modals to Express Necessity, Duty, and Advice"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use a variety of modals to talk about what is necessary, what someone is responsible for and to give advice. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Let's look at the modals <span class=\"italic\">must, have to, have got to, </span>and <span class=\"italic\">should</span>. <br/><br/>  You use the modal <span class=\"italic\">must</span> when we decide for ourselves what is necessary.<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">must</span> show them I can live up to their expectations. </span><br/><br/>  You use <span class=\"italic\">have to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">have got to</span> before verbs that talk about necessity. <span class=\"italic\">Have got to</span> is more casual. <span class=\"italic\">Have to</span> implies that someone else imposed the necessity on you.<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">have to buckle down</span> Kristi, and get it done. <br/> I'<span class=\"strong\">ve got to work</span> systematically.</span><br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Should</span> is a modal you can use to give advice and to talk about duty.<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">should</span> make sure you meet these deadlines. (advice)<br/> You <span class=\"strong\">should</span> take this responsibility seriously.</span> (duty)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I need to make this a quick call. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I've got to work systematically. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You have to buckle down Kristi, and get it done. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You should make sure you meet these deadlines."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I must show them I can live up to their expectations. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I've got to get off the phone."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Questions Within Sentences - Reporting"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use reported speech when you are saying (reporting) what other people said. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you tell people what someone has said in the past, you generally make the verb tense 'more in the past'. You need to change the verb to the next past form. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Direct speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Reported speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI <span class=\\\"strong\\\">like</span> him.\u201d  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">liked</span> him.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m coming</span> to the party.\u201d  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">was coming</span>. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI already <span class=\\\"strong\\\">ate</span>.\u201d\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he had <span class=\\\"strong\\\">already</span> eaten.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI <span class=\\\"strong\\\">can </span>cook.\u201d  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He told me he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">could</span> cook.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cWhere do you <span class=\\\"strong\\\">live</span>?\u201d \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He asked me where I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">lived</span>.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to report questions asked, the subject normally comes before the verb.<br/> <span class=\"underline\">Direct</span>: <span class=\"italic\">When will you be able to have it done by?</span><br/> <span class=\"underline\">Indirect</span>: <span class=\"italic\">He asked when I would be able to have it done by.</span><br/><br/>   When the question is a yes/no questions, you use <span class=\"italic\">if</span> or <span class=\"italic\">whether</span> to report it.<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">He also wondered <span class=\"strong\">if</span> I would be able to do some layout.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "My editor asked me if I could edit two chapters of a manuscript."}, {"type": "example", "content": "He asked when I would be able to have it done by."}, {"type": "example", "content": "He also wondered if I would be able to do some layout."}, {"type": "example", "content": "He asked what kind of experience I had doing layout. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "My editor also asked if I wanted to do photo captions. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Imagine that you and your partner are someone who has just started a new job, and that person's parent."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue for a phone call that takes place between the parent and the employee during the first week at the new job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice your role-play."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Perform your role-play for your class."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write a dialogue between a new employee and their parent."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I give advice and suggestions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I practice a role-play."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le09ob05re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le09ob05re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le09ob05re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Mom</span>: Hello?\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Hi Mom.<br><span class=\"strong\">Mom</span>: Hi Kristy! How's the job going? I was just thinking about you.<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: It's good. I need to make this a quick call. I'm just on lunch.<br><span class=\"strong\">Mom</span>: Well, tell me all about it, the condensed version.<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: I've got a lot of tasks to see through this week. I've got to work systematically. My editor asked me if I could edit two chapters of a manuscript. That's a lot!", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le09ob05re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Mom</span>: You have to buckle down Kristi, and get it done.<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: He asked when I would be able to have it done by and I said I could finish it for Thursday.<br><span class=\"strong\">Mom</span>: You should make sure you meet these deadlines, especially in the beginning.<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Yes, I know Mom. I must show them I can live up to their expectations. He also wondered if I would be able to do some layout. He asked what kind of experience I had doing layout.", "id": 2, "time": "25000", "image": "engenn10le09ob05re2img06.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Mom</span>:  That's great! He's thinking about giving you more accountability. You must have made a good impression.<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: I guess so. But I'm starting to feel overwhelmed. There's so much I need to know. I have to fact-check the manuscript and look for copyright liability. It's exciting but I've got to make sure I don't get in over my head.<br><span class=\"strong\">Mom</span>: Well, it all sounds good. I'm proud of you.<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Thanks Mom. Oh, my editor also asked if I wanted to do photo captions. That would be fun! Okay Mom. I've got to get off the phone. My lunch is over. Talk to you later. Bye!", "id": 3, "time": "50000", "image": "engenn10le09ob05re2img07.jpg"}]}}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can request or report facts about events or actions."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can express necessity, duty, and advice. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about my work responsibilities."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " When you need to talk about work or school issues, who do you call?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What kind of advice do you ask a family member for?"}]}, {"ty